{t: O Holy Night-rev 11-01-2026}
{subtitle: Song:  Original Poem: Placide Cappeau; Song: Adolphe Adam (1847); English Lyrics: John Sullivan Dwight}

{define C#7 frets 1 1 1 2}
{define F#m frets 2 1 2 0}
{comment: Tempo: 84  /  Time: 2/4 with Strum: (d- d-) or Time: 6/8 with Strum: (d- du du d- du du)} 

{comment Verse 1}
[D] O holy night, the [G] stars are brightly [D] shining;
It is the night of the [A7] dear Savior’s [D] birth!
[D] Long lay the world in [G] sin and error [D] pining,
Till He ap-[F#m]peared and the [C#7] soul felt its [F#m] worth.
A [A7] thrill of hope, the [D] weary soul rejoices,
For [A7] yonder breaks a [D] new and glorious morn.

{comment Chorus 1}
[Bm] Fall on your [F#m] knees, O [Em] hear the angel [Bm] voices!
O [D] ni-[A7]ght di-[D]-vine,[G] '  O [D] night [A7] when Christ was [D] born!
O [A7] night, O [D] ho-[G]-ly [D] night [A7], O night di-[D]vine!

{comment Verse 2}
[D] Led by the light of [G] faith serenely [D] beaming,
With glowing hearts by His [A7] cradle we [D] stand.
[D] So led by light of a [G] star sweetly [D] gleaming,
Here came the [F#m] wise men from [C#7] Orient [F#m] land.
The [A7] King of kings lay [D] thus in lowly manger,
In [A7] all our trials [D] born to be our friend!

{comment Chorus 2}
[Bm] Fall on your [F#m] knees, O [Em] hear the angel [Bm] voices!
O [D] ni-[A7]ght di-[D]-vine,[G]  O [D] night [A7] when Christ was [D] born!
O [A7] night, O [D] ho-[G]-ly [D] night [A7], O night di[D] vine!

{comment Verse 3}
[D] Truly He taught us to [G] love one a[D] nother;
His law is love and His [A7] Gospel is [D] peace.
[D] Chains shall He break for the [G] slave is our [D] brother
And in His [F#m] Name all op[C#7] pression shall [F#m] cease.
Sweet [A7] hymns of joy in [D] grateful chorus raise we,
Let [A7] all within us [D] praise His holy Name!

{comment Chorus 3}
[Bm] Fall on your [F#m] knees, O [Em] hear the angel [Bm] voices!
O [D] ni-[A7]ght di-[D]-vine,[G]  O [D] night [A7] when Christ was [D] born!
O [A7] night, O [D] ho-[G]-ly [D] night [A7], O night di[D] vine! [*/(hold)]
